From eb4dde5013eaafe17158983dab71f019645e50f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sergej19882906 <sergej19882906@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:40:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] ramips: mt7621: add IoT Perenio Elegance PEJIR01 support
 for OpenWrt 25.12

Device: Perenio Elegance PEJIR01 (A1 Elegance), MT7621A, 256MB RAM,
128MB NAND, Wi-Fi 2.4 (MT7603) + 5GHz (MT7612), 1xWAN + 2xLAN gigabit,
USB 2.0/3.0, LTE modem GOSUNCN GM510, STM32-controlled RGB LED and
Silicon Labs EFR32 Zigbee via UART mux.

Based on the 21.02 port by sid (koshev-msk), adapted to kernel 6.12:
- DTS: NAND partition map (kernel0/kernel1/ubi/idata), STM32 boot/reset
  GPIO exports, uartlite2/3, DSA switch ports lan1/lan2/wan
- image: dual-kernel factory.bin (stock u-boot web flashing) + sysupgrade
- 02_network: MAC addresses read from the idata MTD partition
- kernel patch: GosunCn GM510 (305a:1415) ECM/NCM USB ID for option.c
- packages: uartmuxd (userspace UART mux -> /dev/umxtty0-2) and
  perenio-mcu (vendor mcu/mcud/stm32flash from stock 9.0.4 firmware)

Tested: full build on OpenWrt v25.12.6; LED via mcud, uartmuxd mux,
wifi kmods, GM510 USB ID verified in option.ko.
